AArch64 SpscQueue
(* Single-producer single-consumer circular buffer (Promising-ARM PLDI'19
   §7 "PCS"): 2 slots at [buf] and [buf,#8], monotone `head`/`tail`
   counters. Producer: wait while tail-head = 2 (LDAR head), STR data,
   STLR tail. Consumer: wait while tail = head (LDAR tail), LDR data,
   STLR head. The producer enqueues 1,2,3 (so slot 0 is reused), the
   consumer dequeues three values into X10,X11,X12.
   Property: the consumer receives 1,2,3 in order. Expected: Always.
   (Threads have different roles: do not use -sym.)
   Proved: `a64_spsc_envG` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64SpscPublic.lean) for all
   layouts, on the low 32 bits, initial head = tail = 0; both threads on the
   cumulative take route (`ThreadRuleRXGS.ofSafelyEnvGTU`, the consumer may
   skip a tail release); per-thread image (each thread runs its own part of
   the code block; the block is `spscProdA ++ spscNop ++ spscConsA`,
   `codeMatches`); concrete instance in A64SpscConcrete.lean.
   Whole image (per-thread deviation resolved): `a64_spsc_envG_whole`
   (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64SpscWholePublic.lean), both threads run this
   whole code block from `prod`/`cons` to `pdone`/`cdone`; concrete
   instance with `runnerMatchesW` in A64SpscWholeConcrete.lean.
   The shared symbols are typed (`uint32_t buf`, slot 0's 4-byte word, slot 1's at `buf+8` undeclared;
   `uint64_t head`, `tail`)
   so that the runner declares them as sized locations at the width of
   the code's accesses (A64DECLS): the runner's
   declarations then agree with the proofs' locations. The code block and
   the verdict are unchanged. Proved from the runner's exact configuration
   (declarations and initial memory included): `a64_spsc_envG_runner`, concrete
   `a64_spsc_envG_runner_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64SpscWholeRunner.lean).
   Proved no fault at the runner's declarations (each access resolves as
   at `decls = {}`): `a64_spsc{P,C}_envG_runner_noFault`, concrete
   `a64_spsc_envG_runner_noFault_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64NoFaultDSpsc.lean).
   Proved program-level fault freedom at the runner's declarations (no
   reachable configuration has a faulting step, any architecture, promises
   included): `a64_spsc_envG_runner_faultFree`, concrete
   `a64_spsc_envG_runner_faultFree_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/A64FaultFreeFixed.lean).
   Proved both at once (safety and fault freedom, at the union of their
   hypotheses): `a64_spsc_envG_runner_safe_faultFree`, concrete
   `a64_spsc_envG_runner_safe_faultFree_concrete` (Promising/SLR/EnvG/RunnerSafeFFA64.lean). *)
# flags:
# expect: Always
{
uint32_t buf=0; uint64_t head=0; uint64_t tail=0;
0:X0=buf; 0:X1=head; 0:X2=tail;
1:X0=buf; 1:X1=head; 1:X2=tail;
}
threads { P0: prod pdone; P1: cons cdone; }
code {
prod:
  MOV W3,#1
  MOV X4,#0
  MOV X7,X0
prod_loop:
  LDAR X5,[X1]
  SUB X6,X4,X5
  CMP X6,#2
  B.EQ prod_loop
  STR W3,[X7]
  EOR X7,X7,#8
  ADD X4,X4,#1
  STLR X4,[X2]
  ADD W3,W3,#1
  CMP W3,#4
  B.NE prod_loop
  B pdone
pdone:
  NOP
cons:
  MOV X4,#0
  MOV X7,X0
c1:
  LDAR X5,[X2]
  CMP X5,X4
  B.EQ c1
  LDR W10,[X7]
  EOR X7,X7,#8
  ADD X4,X4,#1
  STLR X4,[X1]
c2:
  LDAR X5,[X2]
  CMP X5,X4
  B.EQ c2
  LDR W11,[X7]
  EOR X7,X7,#8
  ADD X4,X4,#1
  STLR X4,[X1]
c3:
  LDAR X5,[X2]
  CMP X5,X4
  B.EQ c3
  LDR W12,[X7]
  EOR X7,X7,#8
  ADD X4,X4,#1
  STLR X4,[X1]
  B cdone
cdone:
}
forall (1:X10=1 /\ 1:X11=2 /\ 1:X12=3)
